---
/**
 * Boundary — second biology-lens concept (Single Identity scale).
 * Science-first reading: plasma membrane / selective permeability.
 * Pedagogical order: Gene → Boundary → Cell.
 * Same Space as physics configuration space; Boundary is the membrane aspect.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const osSpaceModel = 'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os/blob/main/docs/space-model.md';
---

<Layout title="Boundary | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Boundary
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					The membrane of the form: the maintained difference between interior and exterior
					that makes a living Identity possible at all.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: cell membrane biology (plasma membrane, selective permeability).
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Pedagogical order with
						<a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>:
						Gene → Boundary → Cell.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Inside only exists because outside is held off.</h2>
				<p>
					In cell biology, the <strong class="text-white/85">plasma membrane</strong> is not packaging around a finished interior.
					It is the condition under which an interior can be maintained at all:
					selective permeability, controlled exchange, continuous work against dissolution into the environment.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, <strong class="text-white/85">Boundary</strong> names that same structural role under the biology lens:
					the maintained difference between what belongs to this Identity and what does not.
					Without Boundary there is no Cell, no protected metabolism, and no place for Gene to found a form that stays distinct.
				</p>
				<p>
					Operationally this is already close to <strong class="text-white/85">Identity Surface</strong>, consent, foreign-estimate zone, and jurisdiction.
					Boundary is the biology-lens name for the membrane condition; Surface is how the OS and the geometric map speak about the same need.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Same Space, next lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Boundary does not replace Space</h2>
				<p>
					<a href="/framework/space" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Space</a>
					(physics lens) names the arena of <strong class="text-white/85">degrees of freedom</strong>.
					Boundary (biology lens) names the <strong class="text-white/85">membrane</strong> of the form that lives in that arena.
					They are not two hosts and not two ontologies. They are two scientific cuts of one Space.
				</p>
				<p>
					<a href="/method" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">IE OS</a>
					implements both cuts in one installable Space: membership and freedom profiles for Identities, plus export, inbound, Surface policy, and grants as membrane work.
					See the Open Core
					<a
						href={osSpaceModel}
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
						class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50"
					>space-model</a>.
				</p>
				<p class="text-base text-white/50">
					Registry remains observer-relative inside each Identity. Boundary is not a shared team perception store.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Boundary is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Membrane condition:</strong> the active separation that creates a usable interior.
						Not a wall only: selective exchange is part of the boundary function.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Jurisdiction edge:</strong> where Ownership and access decisions become meaningful.
						What may enter, what may leave, what is only observed from outside.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prerequisite of Cell:</strong> Gene names what can be passed to found a new form.
						Boundary names what must hold for that form to remain a distinct living unit.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Work, not a static line:</strong> membranes are maintained. Boundaries decay without continuous policy and attention.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Boundary is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not isolation as the goal.</strong>
						A living membrane exchanges. Total closure is death of metabolism, not purity of identity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Stem.</strong>
						Stem is the temporal continuity of one Identity. Boundary is the spatial and jurisdictional condition of the form.
						See <a href="/framework/time" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Time / Identity Stem</a>.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Gene.</strong>
						Gene is the heritable founding configuration passed to a new Identity.
						Boundary is what keeps any Identity (parent or child) distinct while it lives.
						See <a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Cell yet.</strong>
						Cell will name the integrated living unit that has Boundary, carries Gene, and metabolizes.
						Boundary is the membrane condition inside that unit, not the whole unit.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a claim that persons are lipid bilayers.</strong>
						Membrane biology is the science reading. The framework mapping is structural: selective interior, maintained edge, controlled exchange.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a second Space.</strong>
						Boundary is the membrane aspect of Space, not a parallel geometric host.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Gene → Boundary → Cell</h2>
				<p>
					This sequence is <strong class="text-white/85">pedagogical</strong>, not a claim about evolutionary chronology.
				</p>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-4 text-lg">
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Gene</strong> — what can be passed so a new Identity can begin related and still become other.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Boundary</strong> — what must hold so any Identity remains a distinct interior under exchange with the outside.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Cell</strong> (next) — the integrated living unit in which Boundary and Gene co-exist and metabolism runs.
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					In nature, membrane and heritable system are aspects of the cell together.
					In the framework we separate the pages so each role stays sharp: transmission, membrane condition, living unit.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Name the edge:</strong> where does this Identity end, and who decides what crosses?
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prefer selective permeability over total walls:</strong> Interaction must remain possible or the form cannot metabolize reality.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Maintain the membrane:</strong> Boundary is continuous work (policy, consent, attention), not a one-time declaration.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Do not confuse Boundary with Stem:</strong> protecting the edge is not the same as living the full trajectory.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Hold Space and Boundary together:</strong> freedom without membrane dissolves; membrane without freedom freezes the form.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">membrane biology / cell biology</strong>
						(plasma membrane, selective permeability, maintained interior).
						Further concepts (Cell, Metabolism, and interactive signaling) will be founded next.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/space" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Space</a>
					<a href="/framework/gene" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Gene</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/method" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">OS</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
